1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,542
Chapter five — design internals.

2
00:00:03,602 --> 00:00:13,590
So far a node has been one
box with dials. Open it up.

3
00:00:13,650 --> 00:00:20,994
Every node has a subcanvas:
what happens inside the service.

4
00:00:21,054 --> 00:00:30,499
Input, index, algorithm, cache, execution context,
output — the primitives a real engine is made of.

5
00:00:30,559 --> 00:00:38,003
Branch, fan-out, join and loop
wire the control flow between them.

6
00:00:38,063 --> 00:00:42,469
And it runs.

7
00:00:42,529 --> 00:00:55,751
Two hundred ticks through the inner
design — each entity using its own model.

8
00:00:55,811 --> 00:00:59,955
If you disagree with the maths, replace it.

9
00:01:00,015 --> 00:01:08,459
A node-level simulate override runs
your code instead of the built-in model.

10
00:01:08,519 --> 00:01:14,963
Build with AI does the
same job from a sentence.

11
00:01:15,023 --> 00:01:23,468
The execution context on the right
is the worker pool it all runs on.

12
00:01:23,528 --> 00:01:35,444
Change what is inside, and the
outer node’s numbers change with it.

13
00:01:35,504 --> 00:01:40,046
A node is a model. Inside it, another model.

14
00:01:40,106 --> 00:01:44,309
All the way down, and all of it computed.
